  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "**This is the easy version of the problem. The only difference between this and the hard version is that here, you're given the entire array AAA.**\n\nConsider a tree on NNN vertices, with vertex iii having the value AiA_iAi​ associated with it.\n\nThe score of the tree with respect to array AAA, denoted f(A)f(A)f(A), is defined as follows:\n\n\nFor each edge (u,v)(u, v)(u,v) of the tree, give it the value Au+AvA_u + A_vAu​+Av​.\nThe score of the tree is then the greatest common divisor (GCD) of the values of all the edges.\nYou are given a tree on NNN vertices, and an array AAA of length NNN.\n\nCompute the minimum value of f(A)f(A)f(A) across all rearrangements of this array AAA.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_{N}A1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nThe next N−1N-1N−1 lines describe the tree. The iii-th of them contains two space-separated integers uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​, denoting an edge between these two vertices.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the answer on a new line: the minimum possible value of f(A)f(A)f(A) across all rearrangements of AAA.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤2⋅1051 \\leq A_i \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤Ai​≤2⋅105",
      "The input edges describe a tree on the vertex set {1,2,…,N}\\{1, 2, \\ldots, N\\}{1,2,…,N}.",
      "The sum of NNN and the sum of max⁡(A)\\max(A)max(A) across all tests both won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
